    <h1>Stable Diffusion: Generative AI for Visual Media</h1>
    <p>Stable Diffusion is a latent diffusion model developed by researchers at LMU Munich (CompVis) and Stability AI. It was released to the public in 2022 and quickly became a major force in the AI ecosystem.</p>
    
    <h2>What are Diffusion Models?</h2>
    <p>Diffusion models work by slowly adding Gaussian noise to an image until it is unrecognizable, and then learning to reverse the process to "denoise" it back into a meaningful image. This process is surprisingly powerful for generating high-quality images from text prompts.</p>
    
    <h2>Impact and Availability</h2>
    <p>Due to its open-source license and relatively low GPU requirements, Stable Diffusion has been widely adopted by the creative community and has led to a flurry of new tools, plugins, and artistic techniques.</p>

    <p>Search for "Diffusion" or "LMU" in the agent more test results!</p>
